# Pinned ruby-asterism/asterism: the pure Ruby layers of Asterism (the mrbgem
# picoruby-asterism: mrbgem.rake + mrblib/) and the bundled ROS 2 message
# types (data/msgs). doc/ruby_asterism. Same scheme as PICORUBY_TI_PIN:
# - `rake asterism:setup` clones this exact commit into vendor/asterism
#   (gitignored); `rake setup` copies the mrbgem into the picoruby submodule
#   and data/msgs into flash/usr/share/asterism/msgs (gitignored).
# - The repository is public: the clone goes over https, so CI can fetch it.
# - ASTERISM_DIR=<checkout> builds from a working checkout instead (nothing
#   is fetched; rake says when it is not the pinned commit).
# - To update: commit and push asterism's main, put the commit here, run
#   `rake setup` (or any build).
